From c678e6693ec2df750b84c01e82b21aa413bc7665 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravi <ravi@openloopagentics.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:51:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] Add per-button colours and a named palette

Buttons were drawn with two scalar greyscale constants, so there was no way
to express colour at all -- BUTTON_COLOR_INACTIVE: f64 = 0.200 was painted as
set_source_rgb(color, color, color).

Add an Rgb type parsed from #rrggbb, an optional [Palette] table of named
colours, and three optional per-button keys: Color (foreground), Background
and ActiveBackground. Values resolve as a palette name first, then as a hex
literal; an unknown value is reported and ignored rather than fatal, so a typo
during a live config reload cannot take the daemon down.

Colours are resolved in load_config once the palette is known, so the draw
path only ever sees Rgb. With no colour keys set, every button renders exactly
as before.

ButtonConfig also gains Default, which lets the synthetic esc button use
struct update syntax instead of listing every field.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0196XW9vTfjGeWDpHTAmYsws
